<h3>Final model: DeepSeek-V3.2</h3>
<p>After continued pre-training to create the DSA base, DeepSeek ran the full post-training pipeline (specialist distillation + mixed RL training) to produce the final DeepSeek-V3.2. This model achieves parity with GPT-5-High on most reasoning benchmarks while being substantially more cost-efficient to deploy — a direct consequence of DSA reducing the long-context inference cost by ~2.7× at 128K.</p>

<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display: none;" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: DeepSeek Sparse Attention (DSA) Explained</h2>
    <p>DeepSeek-V3.2 introduces DeepSeek Sparse Attention, or DSA — an attention mechanism that reduces the quadratic O(L-squared) complexity of standard attention down to O(L times k), where k is a fixed number of selected tokens much smaller than the sequence length L.</p>
    <p>DSA works in two phases. First, a lightweight "lightning indexer" with few heads and FP8 precision computes a cheap relevance score for every token in the context. This indexer uses a ReLU activation instead of softmax, allowing parallel scoring without a global reduction. Second, only the top-k scoring tokens are passed to the main attention mechanism — at 128K context with k equals 2048, that's attending to just 1.6% of tokens.</p>
    <p>DSA is instantiated under MLA, DeepSeek's latent key-value compression scheme, in MQA mode: a single shared latent vector per selected token is used across all query heads. This is crucial for hardware efficiency — loading one latent vector per selected token saturates memory bandwidth far better than loading per-head tensors.</p>
    <p>Training DSA required two stages of continued pre-training from the existing V3.1 checkpoint. A 2.1-billion-token warm-up stage trained only the indexer on a KL divergence loss against the dense attention distribution. Then a 943-billion-token sparse training stage fine-tuned the full model with top-k selection active, using detached gradients to keep the indexer and main model optimization paths independent.</p>
    <p>The results are compelling: DSA achieves roughly 2.7 times lower inference cost at 128K context, with no measurable quality regression on standard benchmarks and actual improvements on several long-context evaluations.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：DeepSeek稀疏注意力机制详解</h2>
    <p>DeepSeek-V3.2引入了DeepSeek稀疏注意力机制（DSA），将标准注意力的O(L²)二次方复杂度降低至O(L×k)，其中k是远小于序列长度L的固定选择token数量。</p>
    <p>DSA分两个阶段工作。首先，一个轻量级"闪电索引器"通过少量注意力头和FP8精度，为上下文中的每个token计算廉价的相关性分数。该索引器使用ReLU激活而非softmax，允许并行评分而无需全局归约。然后，只有得分最高的前k个token才会传递给主注意力机制——在128K上下文中k=2048时，这意味着只关注1.6%的token。</p>
    <p>DSA在MLA的MQA模式下实例化：每个选定token使用单一共享潜在向量跨所有查询头。这对硬件效率至关重要——每个选定token加载一个潜在向量比加载每头张量更能充分利用内存带宽。</p>
    <p>训练DSA需要从V3.1检查点进行两阶段持续预训练。21亿token的预热阶段仅训练索引器，使用KL散度损失对齐密集注意力分布。然后9437亿token的稀疏训练阶段在top-k选择激活的情况下微调整个模型，通过分离梯度保持索引器和主模型的优化路径独立。</p>
    <p>结果令人信服：DSA在128K上下文下推理成本降低约2.7倍，标准基准测试无明显质量下降，且在多项长上下文评估中实际有所改善。</p>
  </div>
</div>

